{"tag":"1S2E","body":"<div class=\"pq-q ue-math\"><p>An agent chooses between actions <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"x\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"y.\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span> Each yields a certain monetary prize that depends on the state of nature, which is <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span></span></span> with probability <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"α\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"B\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span></span></span> with probability <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"1-α.\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span> The agent maximizes expected utility. Without knowing the state he would choose <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"x;\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">;</span></span></span></span></span> knowing it, he would choose <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"x\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span></span></span> in state <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"y\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span></span></span> in state <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"B.\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span> Discuss the statement: if agent 1 is more risk averse than agent 2, then he is ready to pay more to know the state of nature. Under the expected-utility model, is the statement always true (prove it), always false (prove it), or could it go either way (explain)?</p></div><ol class=\"pq-parts\" role=\"list\"><li class=\"pq-part\"><span class=\"pq-l\">(T1)</span><div class=\"pq-pq\"><div class=\"pq-ans\" data-answer><p class=\"pq-ans-k\">Answer</p><div class=\"ue-math\"><p>It could go either way: more risk aversion neither always raises nor always lowers the amount an agent is ready to pay to learn the state. Readiness to pay is our formulation of the printed phrase.</p></div></div></div></li></ol>"}